    "rawStdout": "TAP version 13\n# Subtest: order aggregation runs a complete saved workflow and persists history\nok 1 - order aggregation runs a complete saved workflow and persists history\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 4.1884\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: branch partitions without mutating input and map reads nested paths\nok 2 - branch partitions without mutating input and map reads nested paths\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.4565\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: rejects cycles, disconnected nodes, unsafe property paths and unknown operators\nok 3 - rejects cycles, disconnected nodes, unsafe property paths and unknown operators\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.3563\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: execution failures are retained and delete removes listing\nok 4 - execution failures are retained and delete removes listing\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.4021\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: reserved identifiers cannot mutate execution result prototypes\nok 5 - reserved identifiers cannot mutate execution result prototypes\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.0958\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: real disk store persists workflows and runs using host-compatible record keys\nok 6 - real disk store persists workflows and runs using host-compatible record keys\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 14.9127\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: invalid non-branch output ports reject before silently discarding records\nok 7 - invalid non-branch output ports reject before silently discarding records\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.2157\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: aggregate overflow produces a retained failed run rather than serialized null\nok 8 - aggregate overflow produces a retained failed run rather than serialized null\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.8637\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: aggregate aliases support nested paths and cannot overwrite metadata\nok 9 - aggregate aliases support nested paths and cannot overwrite metadata\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 0.2949\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: HTTP supports all seven documented methods, JSON/raw bodies, headers, query and from references\nok 10 - HTTP supports all seven documented methods, JSON/raw bodies, headers, query and from references\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 60.6262\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: HTTP retries failing statuses per item and preserves each failed attempt in history\nok 11 - HTTP retries failing statuses per item and preserves each failed attempt in history\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 24.3517\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: HTTP timeout covers delayed headers and a stalled response body, with bounded retries\nok 12 - HTTP timeout covers delayed headers and a stalled response body, with bounded retries\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 122.6341\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: HTTP handles redirects, explicit text format and Never Error while JSON failures stay visible\nok 13 - HTTP handles redirects, explicit text format and Never Error while JSON failures stay visible\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 19.2849\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: HTTP response limits stop retries and record the failed step\nok 14 - HTTP response limits stop retries and record the failed step\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 11.2321\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: HTTP stops accumulating responses when the node output reaches its bounded size\nok 15 - HTTP stops accumulating responses when the node output reaches its bounded size\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 26.8652\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: run secrets and sensitive request/response headers never appear in persisted history, including echoed bodies\nok 16 - run secrets and sensitive request/response headers never appear in persisted history, including echoed bodies\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 14.2769\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: error-output routes failed items away from success output; continue passes last input onward\nok 17 - error-output routes failed items away from success output; continue passes last input onward\n  ---\n  duration_ms: 5.1685\n  type: 'test'\n  ...\n# Subtest: credentials